skills-lock.json

# Personal operational notes. They hold deployment specifics, credentials and
# study notes rather than project code, and are kept out of the repository by
# choice.
#
# Patterns rather than filenames, and that is not tidiness. This list named two
# specific files, and a third — sla-desk-secrets-runbook.md — appeared later and
# was not covered by either. It was caught before any commit, but only because
# `git status` was read carefully; a list of exact names has to be updated by
# whoever creates the next one, and that person is busy writing down a secret.
*runbook*.md
*cheatsheet*.md
*secrets*.md
docs/deploy-runbook.md
